<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan Pieterszoon Coen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1587">1587</a>–<a href="/years/1629">1629</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Coen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan Pieterszoon Coen was an officer and Governor-General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in the early seventeenth century. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavia">Batavia</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in 1619 as the company's headquarters. He also led the violent conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banda-islands">Banda Islands</a> in 1621 to secure the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nutmeg">nutmeg</a> trade, a notorious episode in the history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jan-pieterszoon-coen.jpg" alt="Jan Pieterszoon Coen" width="312" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacques Waben · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Pieterszoon_Coen_by_Jacob_Waben.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The spice monopolies enforced across the Maluku Islands, covering nutmeg, cloves and mace, were maintained through deliberate violence, including the Dutch conquest of the Banda Islands under <b>Jan Pieterszoon Coen</b> in 1621, with the near-extermination and enslavement of their population.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>…again in 1629 Agung sent large armies against Batavia, the base of the Dutch East India Company under <b>Jan Pieterszoon Coen</b>, but both sieges failed; in 1629 Dutch ships destroyed the rice stores gathered for the army at Tegal and Cirebon, and thousands of soldiers died of hunger…</blockquote><a href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram Sultanate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…the trade and conquests of the Dutch East India Company and the Dutch West India Company: in 1621 <b>Jan Pieterszoon Coen</b> had almost all the inhabitants of the Banda Islands massacred, and in the Atlantic slave trade Dutch ships carried more than 550,000 people to the Americas in…</blockquote><a href="/societies/dutch-republic">Social Hierarchy of the Dutch Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1619 <b>Jan Pieterszoon Coen</b> seized Jayakarta and founded Batavia as its headquarters.</blockquote><a href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company territories</a></li></ul></section>
